 respiratory protection that Table 1 specifies for that task, unless the employer instead assesses and limits exposure under 1926.1153(d) (1926.1153(c)(1)). For stationary masonry saws (Table 1 entry (i)) and for handheld power saws of any blade diameter (Table 1 entry (ii)), Table 1 requires a saw equipped with an integrated water delivery system that continuously feeds water to the blade, operated and maintained in accordance with the manufacturer's instructions to minimize dust emissions; the handheld entry additionally requires respiratory protection with an assigned protection factor of 10 when used indoors or in an enclosed area, and for more than four hours per shift outdoors. Where a task is not listed on Table 1, or where the employer does not fully and properly implement the Table 1 controls, the employer must instead ensure no employee is exposed above the permissible exposure limit of 50 micrograms per cubic metre of respirable crystalline silica as an 8-hour time-weighted average, and must assess exposures accordingly (1926.1153(d)(1)-(2)).","jurisdictionProvenance":"USER_CONFIRMED"}],"observationFragment":"a worker is dry-cutting concrete block with a handheld saw","possibleOverlapWith":[],"requiresHumanReview":false}],"version":"v1","hazardCount":1,"evidenceGaps":[],"routingNotes":["Decomposed fragment \"a worker is dry-cutting concrete block with a handheld saw\" routed to silica_respirable_dust"],"isMultiHazard":false,"primaryHazard":{"domainId":"silica_respirable_dust","hazardId":"haz-1","mechanism":"dry cutting/grinding of silica-bearing material","confidence":0.6,"evidenceGaps":[],"hazardFamily":"silica","conditionState":"ACTIVE","correctionStatus":"not_stated","temporalEvidence":[],"reviewerQuestions":[],"supportingSignals":["dry cutting/grinding of silica-bearing material"],"standardCandidates":[{"title":"Respirable crystalline silica","family":"OSHA Construction respirable crystalline silica","status":"UNKNOWN","citation":"29 CFR 1926.1153","s